+## Local customization: automatic completion by default
+
+Bare spawns and profiles without lifecycle settings are now autonomous: a normal
+completed run writes the existing done handshake, returns its final summary, and
+closes its pane without requiring the model to call `subagent_done`. This uses
+Pi's lifecycle hook, not a timer or a guess based on the terminal being idle.
+Explicit `interactive: true` (or profile `auto-exit: false`) keeps a session open;
+explicit `interactive: false` enables automatic completion regardless of profile.
+Both spawn and resume scripts explicitly export the resolved auto-exit flag so
+nested children do not inherit the wrong setting. Errors, Escape/abort, and
+outstanding nested children are not mislabeled as successful completion.
+
+Restart/reload the parent before launching new children. Existing children retain
+their old settings. This is a local patch; review/reapply it after package updates.
+
